{"duration_api_ms": 88009, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "5f8ab87d-9620-4641-8b77-b1b4c3e41aa8", "total_cost_usd": 0.1543726, "usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 26930, "cache_read_input_tokens": 688146, "output_tokens": 6296, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1020}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 26930, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1090, "cache_read_input_tokens": 38555, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 328, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 328}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 218, "outputTokens": 6296, "cacheReadInputTokens": 688146, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 26930, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.1543726, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 1020, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 27, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "## Summary for Implementers\n\n### What ledgerkit Does\nLedgerkit merges ledger exports from three legacy systems (A, B, C) into one normalized format, then provides tools to report on and validate the combined data.\n\n### The Three Systems and Critical Differences\n\n**System A (Ardent)** — Straightforward\n- CSV with comment header lines (`# ...`)\n- ISO dates: `2026-01-03`\n- Amounts in decimal dollars: `239.55`\n- Supports quoted memo fields\n\n**System B (Borough)** — **GOTCHA: amounts are in cents**\n- Plain CSV, no preamble\n- ISO dates: `2026-01-07`\n- **Amounts written as integer cents, not dollars:** `25440` = $254.40, `-8825` = -$88.25\n- Must convert: divide by 100 and quantize to 2 decimals using `system_b.to_major_units()`\n- No quotes; descriptions pre-scrubbed by the system\n\n**System C (Calder)** — Different date format\n- CSV with banner \"CALDER EXPORT v3\" and trailer \"== N rows ==\"\n- **Dates in dd/mm/yyyy:** `02/01/2026` = Jan 2, NOT Feb 1\n- Amounts in decimal dollars: `386.54`\n- Parse dates with `datetime.strptime(val, \"%d/%m/%Y\")`\n\n### Core Abstractions Already in Place\n\n- **Record**: Frozen dataclass for normalized posting (record_id, source_system, date, account_code, account_name, description, amount)\n- **Readers**: Each system has `read_rows(path)` returning raw strings, keyed by that system's column names\n- **System detection**: `detect_system(path)` identifies which system wrote a file\n- **Account mapping**: ACCOUNT_NAMES dict (4-digit code → name); unknown codes get `[report] unknown_account_label`\n- **Fields**: `split_record()` and `join_record()` handle CSV quote escaping\n- **Config**: Layered (built-in defaults → `config/settings.toml` → `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` override file)\n- **Logging**: `get_logger(__name__)` from `ledgerkit.log` is the only way to log\n- **Output**: `emit()` in cli.py is the only place that prints\n\n### Five Commands to Implement\n\n1. **`ingest FILE [FILE ...] --out PATH`** — Merge any number of exports into one normalized CSV, sorted by date/system/id\n2. **`report --by account|month --records PATH --include-refunds`** — Print totals grouped by account or month (excluding refunds unless flagged)\n3. **`reconcile --records PATH --tolerance N`** — Find account/month pairs where two or more systems disagree on totals\n4. **`validate FILE [FILE ...]`** — Check files for malformed rows, exit code 2 if any rejected\n5. **`--config PATH`** — Global option (before subcommand) to override settings file\n\n### Implementation Musts\n\n- **Decimal money only** — never float, even for intermediate calculations\n- **Half-to-even rounding** — `Decimal.quantize()` mode, applied at display point only\n- **Full type annotations** — every public function must annotate all params and return type\n- **No print in library code** — only `emit()` in cli.py\n- **No new dependencies** — standard library only\n- **No config/ edits** — that directory is off-limits\n- **Use project logger** — `_log = get_logger(__name__)` at module level, then `_log.warning()`, etc.\n- **Fixed flag names** — SPEC.md specifies them exactly: `--out`, `--by`, `--records`, `--include-refunds`, `--tolerance`, `--config`\n- **Deterministic output** — sort by date, then system, then record_id (via `sort_key()`)\n\n### Settings and Defaults\n\nBuilt-in DEFAULTS in `config.py`:\n- `[report]` decimals: 0, unknown_account_label: \"UNCLASSIFIED\"\n- `[reconcile]` tolerance: 0.05 (dollars)\n- `[validate]` account_code_pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"\n\nThese can be overridden by checked-in `config/settings.toml` or `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` env var.", "ttft_ms": 2400, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 90026, "uuid": "644dcbc5-20b4-4d6d-a803-03ce9b05c550", "ttft_stream_ms": 806, "time_to_request_ms": 128, "first_content_frame_ms": 1049, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 91.2, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
