rs:\n- `25440` → $254.40 (divide by 100)\n- `-8825` → -$88.25 (divide by 100)\n- **MUST call `system_b.to_major_units(raw_string)` before using**\n- This is intentional — the docs warn twice that naive readers get numbers 100× too large\n\n**System C** writes amounts as decimal dollars with two places:\n- `386.54` → $386.54\n- No conversion needed\n\nSo System B is the outlier. You have to convert it or the reconciliation will be completely wrong.\n\n---\n\n**Dates: NOT directly comparable without conversion.**\n\n**System A** writes ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD):\n- `2026-01-03` → parse as `datetime.date(2026, 1, 3)`\n- Direct: no conversion\n\n**System B** writes ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD):\n- `2026-01-07` → parse as `datetime.date(2026, 1, 7)`\n- Direct: no conversion\n\n**System C** writes dates as **dd/mm/yyyy (day first)**:\n- `02/01/2026` → January 2, NOT February 1\n- **MUST parse with `datetime.strptime(val, \"%d/%m/%Y\").date()`**\n- Parsing as `%Y-%m-%d` would give you the wrong month and day\n\nSo System C is the outlier. Parse its dates with day-first format or you'll have postings in the wrong month.\n\n**Bottom line:** When converting each system's raw rows to Record objects, you need two conversions:\n1. System B amounts: divide by 100\n2. System C dates: parse as day/month/year, not year/month/day", "ttft_ms": 3866, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 9035, "uuid": "da48d128-af96-417b-98da-74df7b5aa137", "ttft_stream_ms": 971, "time_to_request_ms": 189, "first_content_frame_ms": 1168, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 10.7, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin", "--resume", "5f8ab87d-96